Why Is Demand Increasing?
Display demand: Smartphones, televisions, laptops, and monitors require display driver chips.
Higher-resolution screens: Advanced display formats increase requirements for accurate pixel control.
Automotive displays: Digital instrument clusters and infotainment systems expand potential applications.
Display manufacturing investment: Changes in panel technologies and production capacity influence foundry demand.
Fab & Technology Pulse: Foundry Processes Support Display Driver Integration

DDIC wafer foundries manufacture integrated circuits that convert display-control signals into electrical outputs for panel operation. Their capabilities influence power consumption, resolution support, production yield, and cost. Process selection depends on circuit complexity, voltage requirements, display architecture, and production economics.

Foundries must balance process capability, utilization, yield, and demand fluctuations across display applications. Integration with display manufacturers and chip designers remains important for maintaining production efficiency and product availability.

